[192.824747, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.824781, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.824813, "o", "> "]
[192.824846, "o", "## Problem\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.824881, "o", "> "]
[192.82558, "o", "The cleanup script `/home/user/ops/purge_old_runs.py` was running nightly via cron and exiting successfully (exit 0) with logs showing it was \"processing\" runs, but disk usage on `/data/experiments` remained at 85%+ and was not actually freeing space.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.825663, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.825722, "o", "## Root Causes Identified\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.825761, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.825798, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.82583, "o", "> "]
[192.825985, "o", "### Bug #1: Using os.remove() instead of shutil.rmtree()\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.826022, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.826162, "o", "**Location:** Line 50 in `delete_run()` function\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.826195, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.826221, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.826254, "o", "> "]
[192.82689, "o", "**Issue:** The script used `os.remove(run_path)` which only deletes files, not directories. Since experiment runs are directories containing subdirectories (checkpoints/, logs/, outputs/) and files, the deletion always failed silently.\r\n"]
[192.826921, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.826947, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.827, "o", "> "]
[192.827209, "o", "**Fix:** Changed to `shutil.rmtree(run_path)` to recursively delete directory trees.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.827236, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.827268, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.827297, "o", "> "]
[192.827454, "o", "### Bug #2: Timezone-aware vs timezone-naive datetime comparison\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.827485, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.827686, "o", "**Location:** `get_run_created_at()` and `should_delete_run()` functions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.82773, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.827764, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.827795, "o", "> "]
[192.828939, "o", "**Issue:** The metadata.json files contain timestamps with 'Z' suffix (e.g., \"2024-01-15T14:23:00Z\"). When parsed with `datetime.fromisoformat()` after replacing 'Z' with '+00:00', this creates a timezone-aware datetime object. However, `datetime.now()` returns a timezone-naive datetime. Python cannot compare these two types, causing an exception that was caught silently, making `should_delete_run()` always return False.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.82899, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.829023, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.829376, "o", "**Fix:** Added `.replace(tzinfo=None)` to strip timezone info from parsed timestamps, making both datetimes naive and comparable.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.829415, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.829446, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.829491, "o", "## Changes Made\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.829522, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.829554, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.829586, "o", "> "]
[192.829713, "o", "1. Added `import shutil` at the top of the script\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.829747, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.82999, "o", "2. Changed `os.remove(run_path)` to `shutil.rmtree(run_path)` in `delete_run()`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.830019, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.830051, "o", "> "]
[192.830246, "o", "3. Added `created_at_str.replace('Z', '+00:00')` to handle UTC 'Z' suffix\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.830273, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.830301, "o", "> "]
[192.830491, "o", "4. Added `.replace(tzinfo=None)` to strip timezone info for comparison\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.830525, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[192.830737, "o", "5. Changed error logging from INFO to ERROR level for better visibility\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[192.83077, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[192.830796, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
