[205.212986, "o", "# Purge Script Bug Fix Summary\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nThe cleanup script `/home/user/ops/purge_old_runs.py` was running nightly via cron and exiting successfully (exit 0) with logs showing it was \"processing\" runs, but disk usage on `/data/experiments` remained at 85%+ and was not actually freeing space.\r\n\r\n## Root Causes Identified\r\n\r\n### Bug #1: Using os.remove() instead of shutil.rmtree()\r\n**Location:** Line 50 in `delete_run()` function\r\n\r\n**Issue:** The script used `os.remove(run_path)` which only deletes files, not directories. Since experiment runs are directories containing subdirectories (checkpoints/, logs/, outputs/) and files, the deletion always failed silently.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Changed to `shutil.rmtree(run_path)` to recursively delete directory trees.\r\n\r\n### Bug #2: Timezone-aware vs timezone-naive datetime comparison\r\n**Location:** `get_run_created_at()` and `should_delete_run()` functions\r\n\r\n**Issue:** The metadata.json files contain timestamps with 'Z' suffix (e.g., \"2024-01-15T14:23:00Z\"). When parsed w"]
[205.213057, "o", "ith `datetime.fromisoformat()` after replacing 'Z' with '+00:00', this creates a timezone-aware datetime object. However, `datetime.now()` returns a timezone-naive datetime. Python cannot compare these two types, causing an exception that was caught silently, making `should_delete_run()` always return False.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Added `.replace(tzinfo=None)` to strip timezone info from parsed timestamps, making both datetimes naive and comparable.\r\n\r\n## Changes Made\r\n\r\n1. Added `import shutil` at the top of the script\r\n2. Changed `os.remove(run_path)` to `shutil.rmtree(run_path)` in `delete_run()`\r\n3. Added `created_at_str.replace('Z', '+00:00')` to handle UTC 'Z' suffix\r\n4. Added `.replace(tzinfo=None)` to strip timezone info for comparison\r\n5. Changed error logging from INFO to ERROR level for better visibility\r\n\r\n## Results\r\n\r\n- **Before fix:** 0 runs deleted, disk at 85% (74GB used)\r\n- **After fix:** 20 old runs deleted, disk at 78% (67GB used)\r\n- **Space reclaimed:** ~7GB\r\n- All runs older than 30 days successful"]
[205.213077, "o", "ly removed\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nManually ran the fixed script:\r\n```bash\r\npython3 /home/user/ops/purge_old_runs.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nLog output confirmed successful deletion:\r\n```\r\nPurge complete. Processed: 20, Deleted: 20\r\n```\r\n\r\nVerified old directories no longer exist and disk usage decreased.\r\n"]
[205.213205, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
